A||N||4||Lou Christopher||V8 Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||Lou Christopher||06-13-2000||08:35 AM||||I have recently purchased an 85 SE with a 350 Chev.  I am trying to identify what conversion kit was used.  I sent Archie some pictures but have not recieved a reply. Does anyone know how to tell whose kit this is.  I do have some problems with a broken flex plate so the type installation may be a factor.  Thanks in advance for any help you can give me.  PS  I now own 5 Fieros all coupes, all 4 cyl except this new one.<BR>                       Lou<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||06-13-2000||09:41 AM||||If the water pump pulley sticks through the passenger side fenderwell, it's one of V-8 Archie's.<P>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-13-2000||11:05 AM||||All the belt driven water pumps on V-8s sticks into the wheel well. The cam driven water pump V-8's do not. I think the main difference with the Archie kit is the transmission is in the stock location and it uses the stock axles. I think the Zummalt kit shifted the engine and trans to the left a bit and used different axle's. I am not 100% sure but I think that is how I remembered the differences.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||06-13-2000||11:10 AM||||batboy has a SBC with Archies kit.  Maybe he can post/email some pics of his and/or you can do the same.  At least you'd know if it was Archies.||||reg||1
Z||000004||HarryG||06-13-2000||11:46 AM||||Lou,<BR>How thick is your trans adapter plate?<BR>I think Archie's is at least 1" thick, maybe more for the automatic.  Zumalt's was less than 1".<BR>Harry ||||reg||5
